 "MUSIC", "catalogNbr": "3318", "type": "C"}, {"subject": "PMA", "catalogNbr": "3418", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "08/25/2025", "sessionEndDt": "12/20/2025", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "This course surveys the histories, aesthetics, and politics of music and virtuality, focusing on contemporary manifestations of \u201cvirtual music\u201d since the 2010s. We will learn about how music is created, performed, and consumed in virtual environments, focusing specifically on questions of embodiment and identity. Case studies will include virtual and augmented reality concerts; musical performances in video games; virtual bands; and Web3/blockchain music. We will pay particular attention to the ties between virtual worlds, musical aesthetics, and queer and trans community building. Students will learn how to conduct digital musical ethnography and will complete participant observation-based final projects in a virtual music community. (HC)", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": null, "catalogEnrollmentPriority": "", "catalogLang": null, "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": null, "catalogAttribute": null, "catalogWhenOffered": null, "catalogComments": null, "catalogPrereqCoreq": null, "catalogPrereq": "", "catalogCoreq": "", "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": null, "catalogPermission": null, "catalogCourseSubfield": null, "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "catalogName": null, "catalogNextOffered": null, "lastTermsOffered": "2025FA", "catalogCredits": null, "catalogGradeOption": null, "catalogLocation": null, "catalogCrosslisted": null, "catalogCrosslistings": null, "catalogComeets": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2909, "crseId": 374074, "crseOfferNbr": 6, "subject": "LGBT", "catalogNbr": "3555", "titleShort": "Comics as a Medium", "titleLong": "Comics as a Medium", "crseAttrs": [{"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "CA-AG", "descr": "AG-Cultural An